  "title": "Battle of Sekigahara",
  "summary": "On 21 October 1600 at Sekigahara in Mino Province, Tokugawa Ieyasu's Eastern Army defeated Ishida Mitsunari's Western Army after defections, including that of Kobayakawa Hideaki, broke the Western line around noon. Mitsunari was later captured and executed. Ieyasu was appointed shogun and the Tokugawa shogunate ruled Japan until 1868.",
